================================================================================
MCP: dedicated compute_virtual_attributes tool for virtual attribute values
================================================================================

Context
-------
Virtual attribute declarations already rode along with `get_entity_context`, and
values could be obtained with `compute_virtual_attributes=True`, but that flag
sat on a broad context tool — easy to miss when a user asks "what is the risk
score of customer C-42?". Actions already had a dedicated verb
(`invoke_entity_action`); virtual attributes did not.

Changes
-------
1. `src/mcp-server/server/app.py` — added `compute_virtual_attributes(entity_uri,
   function?)` MCP tool calling `GET /api/v1/digitaltwin/nodes/virtual-attributes`.
   Docstring states explicitly: call this when the user asks about a virtual
   attribute value. Hints in `describe_entity` and `get_entity_context` now
   point at this tool instead of the inline flag.
2. `src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py` — external REST endpoint
   `GET /api/v1/digitaltwin/nodes/virtual-attributes` (same allow-list and MCP
   policy enforcement as the internal `/dtwin/nodes/virtual-attributes` route).
3. `src/back/core/mcp_tools.py` — registered the tool in the domain-scoped MCP
   catalog (eighth configurable tool).
4. `.planning/virtual-attributes/SPEC.md`, `tests/eval/datasets/mcp/virtual_attributes.jsonl`,
   documentation (`mcp.md`, `api.md`, `features.md`, `user-guide.md`,
   `data-access.md`, `README.md`) — updated tool surface and eval constraints.
5. Tests — MCP gating, formatting, external API, and MCP catalog guards.

